\f1\fs22 Halo fought his way to the amenities corridor using a silver service tray as a shield and blunt-bladed weapon. Even the fury of the Elvi was no match for his fighting skill. As for the Airborne, they were too easy.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The timing was perfect. Sarah emerged from the toilets as Halo entered the corridor. He nodded at her and smiled professionally; she reciprocated. The passed each other. Halo whirled, threw his arm over her shoulder and twisted her over his extended thigh and threw her off balance. He muffled her cries with his other hand.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Off her feet and cradled under her assailant\'92s arm, Sarah\'92s worked her feet to regain purchase of the polished floor. She twisted her torso and grabbed at the attacker\'92s arms, but his shock-and-awe tactics had her off balance without leverage. She tried biting his hand as he dragged her, but the way he covered her mouth was too expert. Sarah almost panicked as she realised she was in the hands of a professional killer.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo felt her stop fighting, which seemed all too easy, but incredibly thrilling. Elation pumped his heart and breaths of victory filled his lungs. Everything was perfect. There was a hover-copt waiting on a pad 20 floors below. He was already savouring how he\'92d planned it. In the living room of a safe house he\'92d set up the perfect altar. A king-size mattress ensemble in the centre of the room was covered with a white, waterproof sheet that would allow her blood to flow and pool. Dozen of squat, fat candles stood on black pedestals, armed with electrostatic devices so he could light them all at once with a tap on tablet. Tall narrow mirrors leaned against the walls and were angled perfectly for him to view his performance from every angle. There were tiny cameras stuck to every surface\'97more than you\'92d find in a small prison. Attached to the bed was an intricate array of belts and buckles and ropes and chains for restraining her just so. It would be perfect. He\'92d been diligent. He knew every dimension of every part of her body. Once strapped in, she\'92d be in the perfect position and at the perfect height. And with mirrors positioned by the edge of the bed, he\'92d be able to look into her eyes, and she\'92d be able to see the 
\f2\i Slice of Life
\f1\i0  raised then come down. He\'92d never know what she\'92d see after that, be he hoped it would be more.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo awarded himself a smile as he pressed the call button for a service elevator that would take him to the hover-pad stalk. The doors immediately opened.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley\'92s first impulse was to call for back-up, then realised every Airborne in the restaurant would have, on immediate beckon and call, their own private security that would be immeasurably more effective than the police force. Then she realised the Airborne were mostly bemused spectators. The fighting was almost exclusively among the Elvi, with a few younger Airborne throwing in for the sport of it.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Then Hayley realised Sarah was nowhere in the restaurant. She hadn\'92t returned from her comfy break.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo threw her into the lift, stepped in and turned to punch the floor button for the hover-pad stalk. His satisfied smile faded when he saw her shoes on the floor almost a metre away in the hall. He stood, frozen by indecision. His professionalism did not permit him to leave such clumsy clues behind. He tried to reach for the shoes without stepping out of the lift.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah recovered quickly and stealthily regained her feet and, while her assailant stared at her shoes. She hooked her foot in front of his calf and gave him a mighty shove. He tripped and fell out of the elevator. Sarah pushed the door 
\fs18 CLOSE
\fs22  button and the doors responded. The attacker thrust his foot over the threshold; the doors jerked to a halt and retreated.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo regained his feet with the speed of a cat and launched at her. It was a feint designed to make her cower and give him the split second he needed to order the lift down to the hover-pad stalk. But she didn\'92t cower but received his assault within her space, grabbed his arm and redirected the force while twisting. Halo\'92s eyes almost popped with the pain; it felt like she\'92d wrenched his arm from his shoulder as easily as pulling a wing off an overcooked chicken. He dropped and rolled, and kicked her calf. She buckled and fell. Two long sharp fingernails came directly for his eyes. He reflexively turned his head, and received shallow bloody lines gouged across his face. With all his might, he thrust up to regain his feet. She fell back. Halo whirled and spun, came to one knee, then to his feet, and backed into a corner. She did the same almost as fast and backed into the corner by the control panel. She pushed the 
\fs18 ALARM
\fs22  button. Halo was running out of time. He growled and set himself for a proper fight. She had surprised him, but now there would be no mercy. He came at her as if his life depended on it, but every thrust, parry and block, she had an answer for, and she was quick. With the cold processing of a killer, he assessed his adversary as they fought. Even a little messed up, she was still beautiful and vital. The colour of her skin was perfect, her lips flush and full. She looked as if she could fight for hours and still be in perfect health.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Perfect health. What was it with this woman? Was there more to her than the intense attraction and the compulsion to have her that she made him feel? She was fighting him with such speed and accuracy; did she possess perfect reaction time as well as perfect health? Was she too fast and skilled for him? Who was this woman? Was she a woman at all?\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo realised, as they fought, it was he who was taking a beating. Parts of his body, bone and muscle, organ and sinew, were complaining of injury. Then something in his knee snapped. It took all his training to remain on his feet.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>And that\'92s when he took the 
\f2\i Slice of Life
\f1\i0  from his pocket.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony was not as quick as Hayley, partly because he was too busy throwing punches which, though some landed, were hardly widow-makers. Yet the Elvi who received his blows were so ashamed of being clocked by the Great Teacher, they retired from the m\'eal\'e9e.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>While he was catching his breath, he noticed. \'91Sarah!\'92 he called out. He saw Hayley run to the services corridor and ran after her. \'92The Holy Momma!\'92 he called to the the Elvi. \'91With me!\'92\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The Elvi dropped what they were doing\'97which is to say, punching the lights out of each other\'97and followed the Great Teacher.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony gained sight of the service lifts as Hayley picked up a shoe, which was one of a pair lying before an elevator.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander heard Tony cry out, \'91Sarah!\'92 and storm out of the restaurant with a contingent of Elvi following.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Come on,\'92 Eloise ordered her son and, with the calm assurance of an immortal, followed Tony.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Alexander took a little longer while he decided which camera crews he should take with him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Halo struck and buried the 
\f2\i Slice of Life
\f1\i0  deep into her chest. At least, that\'92s what his brain reported until his scrambled senses reported the more accurate information that she had parried the blow, stepped to the side, wrenched his wrist and forced him to drop the weapon. Halo\'92s visioned cleared and saw her standing with weight distributed evenly on the balls of her feet, the 
\f2\i Slice of Life
\f1\i0  held easily in her hand, its point eyeing him warily. He had now now she could strike swiftly if he gave her an excuse. Then Halo heard a 
\f2\i bing
\f1\i0  and the doors opened. He turned to make an escape.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Hayley pressed the lift button and was surprised to see the lift doors open. A waiter rushed out at her. No, not a waiter. Recognising Haloren Smythe, suspected Nightclub Vampire, she firmly shoved him in the chest and sent him back into the elevator. \'91Going somewhere, sport?\'92 she said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah saw her attacker lurched out of the lift then reverse, his centre of gravity at greater speed than his feet. He collided with her. Her hand felt wet and slick. Shock bolted through her as she saw blood spurting all over her belly. The 
\f2\i Slice of Life
\f1\i0  was buried fully in her assailant\'92s back just below his rib cage.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Tony saw the lift open and Halo in a waiter\'92s uniform emerge from it. Hayley moved with some kind of force that sent Halo backwards. His eyes bulged to the size and shape of mandarins and the expanse of his mouth could have admitted an orange. His face became a frozen mask as he fell to his knees and toppled forward, Tony saw the knife in Halo\'92s back before he saw terror-stricken Sarah with blood-slick hands and red-stained torso.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Halo!\'92 Tony called.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91Get Kathy,\'92 Hayley barked at him, but all Tony wanted to do was run to his friend\'92s aide. \
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'91I\'92ll get her, Great Teacher,\'92 one of the Elvi said.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>The High Elvis stood by the open lift with a degree of regal detachment, and hoped no one noticed how miffed he was that we was not allowed to complete his performance.\
