<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah sat and slumped against the back wall of the elevator and contemplated what she\'92d just done. Now, many men in all universes\'97who believe military service and playing rugby and soccer and fulfilling executive business roles and voting and being able to decide what to wear are all too strenuous for the fairer gender of the species\'97these men might expect Sarah to have degenerated into a tropologically female-normative state of emotionally sobbing blubber. But Sarah, in the cold steel reality of life and death, and with indomitable maternal strength, merely thought, 
\f2\i That mother-taxer deserves all he got
\f1\i0 .\
